  "narrative": "The pre-signed estimates make the sign audit important: for each registered claim, values consistently above +0.15 support the claimed direction, while values below -0.15 indicate a meaningful opposite raw direction. H7 (KEAP1 loss, positive direction) has signed estimate +0.832 with interval +0.766 to +0.897, far exceeding the 0.15-unit threshold; I accept it as a scientifically meaningful positive association in this dataset. H8 (SMARCA4 loss, negative direction) has signed estimate +0.833 with interval +0.767 to +0.898, which means the raw exposed-minus-comparator difference is strongly negative; I accept this as a meaningful negative association. H1 (TP53 loss, negative direction) shows signed estimate -0.423, interval -0.520 to -0.327. This is not a null result but a strong opposite raw association, so the original negative claim is rejected and a reversed positive claim is registered. The remaining genetic and marker comparisons are either near zero or have intervals that do not support a threshold-level effect in the claimed direction; they are rejected as not scientifically meaningful in this dataset. Multiplicity across 12 initial comparisons is not decisive for H7/H8 because their intervals are far beyond the threshold, but it supports careful follow-up. H7 and H8 may still be confounded by co-mutation patterns, lineage subtype, screen batch, or assay construction, so I request independent validation for H7 and register targeted stratification tests. These tests examine whether KEAP1 and SMARCA4 associations persist excluding relevant co-mutations and within adenocarcinoma, and whether the null STK11 effect is masked by KEAP1 co-occurrence. They also register the strong TP53 reversal for direct analysis. These are associations in the supplied data, not causal or generalizable effects.",
  "research_notes": "Initial binary screen: strong accepted effects are KEAP1_loss positive (R7) and SMARCA4_loss negative (R8). TP53_loss is strongly opposite to the original negative hypothesis (R1); propose reversed TP53_loss claim. Null/not meaningful: KRAS, MYC amplification, EGFR amplification, PIK3CA, overall STK11, ARID1A, and markers d/e/f. Current priority: validation of H7; follow-up subgroup/eligibility analyses for H7/H8 and co-mutation masking of STK11. Interpret accepted results as dataset-level associations only. Later consider continuous signatures, screen-quality strata, and interactions if strong effects remain robust.",
  "validate": "H7"
