  "narrative": "The new triple-exclusion analyses provide strong within-dataset support that the central KEAP1, SMARCA4, PTEN, and TP53 associations are not simple proxies for one another. KEAP1 loss remains a very large positive association with dependency_composite when TP53, SMARCA4, and PTEN loss are excluded: signed estimate +0.809, interval +0.768 to +0.850. Because this claim is positive-direction, this means KEAP1-loss cells have higher composite dependency scores, i.e. weaker composite dependency, by far more than the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept and close this independence context. SMARCA4 loss remains a very large negative raw association, signed +0.816 with interval +0.771 to +0.860 for the negative-direction claim, so SMARCA4-loss cells have substantially more negative dependency scores, i.e. stronger composite dependency, independent of the other three central alterations. This is also far above threshold and is accepted. PTEN loss remains supported after excluding KEAP1, SMARCA4, and TP53: signed +0.252, interval +0.169 to +0.335, with the lower bound above the 0.15 threshold. Thus PTEN-loss-associated stronger dependency is not explained by co-occurrence with those three losses. TP53 loss is also strongly supported in the maximal triple-exclusion context: signed +0.395, interval +0.291 to +0.499, indicating weaker composite dependency in TP53-loss cells relative to TP53-intact cells. Given that TP53 main-effect H13 remains the only central accepted association without independent validation, I request validation for H13 rather than for this triple-exclusion refinement.\n\nCDKN2A remains borderline and not conclusively meaningful. In the triple-exclusion context excluding TP53, SMARCA4, and KEAP1, the signed estimate is +0.144 with interval +0.083 to +0.204; this is just below the 0.15-unit point threshold and its lower bound does not support a threshold-level effect. In high-quality screens, the signed estimate is +0.130 with interval +0.020 to +0.240. The high-quality context therefore does not strengthen the near-threshold signal. These findings keep CDKN2A unresolved rather than accepted. Because the effects are small and borderline, and because independent validation budget is better spent completing the central TP53 association, I keep CDKN2A active but lower priority, with H79 deferred.\n\nThe central-pair interactions are less conclusive. KEAP1 with TP53 shows a positive signed interaction +0.210, interval +0.019 to +0.400; the point exceeds the threshold and the interval excludes zero, but it does not robustly exceed 0.15. Given small interaction cell sizes and multiple testing, I leave it unresolved and active rather than accepting it. KEAP1 with PTEN gives signed +0.145, interval -0.064 to +0.354, just below threshold and compatible with null/opposite directions; unresolved. SMARCA4 with PTEN gives signed -0.107, interval -0.321 to +0.108, which is opposite to the claimed direction and excludes meaningful claimed-direction effects, so I reject and close that context. PTEN with TP53 gives signed -0.157, interval -0.459 to +0.145, also opposite to the claimed direction and not supporting a threshold-level claimed interaction; reject and close.\n\nFor broad exploratory predictors, APC mutation shows signed -0.030, interval -0.114 to +0.054, which is negligible and opposite to the claimed negative direction; reject. BRAF V600E shows signed +0.049, interval -0.071 to +0.169, far below threshold and not supporting a meaningful negative association; reject. Overall, the new evidence sharpens the central dataset landscape: KEAP1 and TP53 losses are associated with weaker composite dependency, while SMARCA4 and PTEN losses are associated with stronger composite dependency, and each remains large or clearly above threshold under stringent triple-exclusion. These are associations in the supplied dataset, not causal effects, not claims of single-gene knockout biology, and not claims of external generalizability. Multiple overlapping discovery contrasts and small interaction cells warrant caution; validation of the main TP53 claim is the highest-priority remaining step.",
