  "narrative": "The two validation response deadlines are confirmatory and materially strengthen the SMARCA4 landscape. For the main SMARCA4-loss claim, independent validation gives a signed estimate of +0.845 with a conservative independent interval from +0.752 to +0.939. Because H8 is negative-direction, this means SMARCA4-loss cells have a lower, more negative dependency_composite value by far more than the 0.15-unit threshold. I therefore accept and close H8. The high-quality-screen SMARCA4 context also validates cleanly: signed estimate +0.809, interval +0.691 to +0.927. This is well above threshold, so H32 remains accepted and closed. These are within-dataset associations; the composite score is not a SMARCA4 knockout measurement and does not imply causal generalization.\n\nThe new validation for H88 changes the CDKN2A assessment. H88 asks whether CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger composite dependency by more than 0.15 after removing TP53, SMARCA4, KEAP1, and PTEN loss. Discovery gave a signed estimate of +0.164 with a lower bound of +0.101. Independent validation, however, gives a smaller signed estimate of +0.121 with a conservative interval from +0.034 to +0.209. The validation direction is supportive, but the point estimate is below the threshold and the lower bound is far below it. Combined with the pattern of other CDKN2A contrasts being near but not threshold-robust, the best current conclusion is that CDKN2A loss may be weakly associated with stronger dependency, but the supplied dataset does not support a scientifically meaningful threshold-level independent association. I therefore leave the claim unresolved rather than falsely accepting it, but close it as low priority because current evidence argues that additional discovery-focused follow-up is unlikely to be more informative than completing broader predictor exploration.\n\nI also close the redundant CDKN2A/MTAP follow-up investigations: main CDKN2A, TP53-intact CDKN2A, TP53/MTAP-intact CDKN2A, triple-exclusion CDKN2A, high-quality full-exclusion CDKN2A, MTAP-intact full-exclusion CDKN2A, and the CDKN2A-by-MTAP interaction. MTAP itself remains much less supported: H97, MTAP loss after excluding the major central losses and CDKN2A, was opposite the claimed direction and far from threshold. Thus the data argue against a strong independent MTAP association or a large CDKN2A-MTAP synergy.\n\nThe central supported dataset landscape is now coherent and extensively tested: KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss are associated with higher dependency_composite values, meaning weaker composite dependency; SMARCA4 loss and PTEN loss are associated with lower, more negative dependency_composite values, meaning stronger composite dependency. KEAP1 and SMARCA4 remain extremely robust after stringent central-loss exclusion, high-quality screen restriction, and adenocarcinoma restriction. TP53 remains robust and independently validated. PTEN remains accepted from its main validated effect and strong central-loss-exclusion contexts, though the exact magnitude near the 0.15 threshold is less certain than for KEAP1 or SMARCA4. Negative or below-threshold findings include KRAS mutation, MYC amplification, EGFR amplification, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A loss in the claimed negative direction, STK11 loss in the claimed negative direction, RB1 loss in the claimed positive direction, SMAD4 loss, APC mutation, BRAF V600E, the three constructed research markers, and MTAP after central-loss exclusion. Remaining uncertainty is mainly confined to modest near-threshold CDKN2A signals, some low-powered interactions, and untested broad predictors such as ERBB2 amplification, BRCA2 loss, NF1 loss, MSI-high, MTAP main effect, and technical/library indicators. The most informative next analyses are therefore to broaden beyond the central mutation set, starting with these untested binary predictors and technical indicators; if any pass threshold, focused follow-up or validation should be requested at the appraise stage. All conclusions remain association findings in the supplied dataset, not causal claims, single-gene knockout claims, or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 5 synthesis final: Validation response deadlines confirmed SMARCA4 main H8 and SMARCA4 high-quality H32; both accepted/closed. CDKN2A full-central validation H88 failed threshold: discovery +0.164 lower +0.101; validation +0.121 interval +0.034 to +0.209. Therefore CDKN2A is not accepted; possible small direction-consistent association but not scientifically meaningful by threshold. Closed CDKN2A/MTAP follow-up cluster (H22, H50, H62, H78, H95, H96, H98) as low priority. MTAP full-central H97 rejected; no strong independent MTAP effect or CDKN2A-MTAP synergy supported. Supported central landscape: KEAP1 loss higher dependency_composite/weaker dependency; TP53 loss higher composite/weaker dependency; SMARCA4 loss lower composite/stronger dependency; PTEN loss lower composite/stronger dependency. Central effects are validated and robust in major contexts. PTEN magnitude is the most threshold-sensitive among central accepted effects. Next analysis priority: broad untested binary predictors and technical indicators rather than more central confirmations. Active registered claims to consider next: H40 ERBB2 amplification, H41 BRCA2 loss, H42 NF1 loss, H43 MSI-high, H23 MTAP main, H24 Avana library, H25 matched RNA/DNA omics; optional additional technical indicators if registered. Keep interactions low priority due small cells unless a main broad predictor passes. Maintain all conclusions as supplied-dataset associations, not causality/generalizability."
}

