  "narrative": "The new validation settles the two due claims. For H120, the independent validation R92 gives a signed MSI-high estimate of +0.802 with an independent interval from +0.635 to +0.969. Both the point estimate and lower bound exceed the 0.15 composite-unit threshold in the claimed direction, and the estimate is essentially unchanged from discovery R73 +0.792. I therefore accept H120 and close the investigation. This supports a large within-supplied-dataset association: MSI-high cells have substantially lower, more negative dependency_composite values, meaning stronger composite dependency, and the effect is not explained by TP53, SMARCA4, KEAP1, or PTEN loss because H121 was also strong in the central-loss-intact population R74. For H88, the independent validation R66 gives a signed CDKN2A-loss estimate of +0.121, interval +0.034 to +0.209, in the context where TP53, SMARCA4, KEAP1, and PTEN losses are all absent. Although R57 was a borderline discovery point +0.164, the validation point is below the threshold and the interval lower bound is far below threshold, while the upper bound only weakly reaches threshold-level values. Taken together, the evidence is consistent with a small directional effect but not with a robust, scientifically meaningful threshold-level association of CDKN2A loss with stronger dependency. I change H88 to reject and close it as a threshold-level claim; this is not proof that no small effect exists, but CDKN2A is not part of the supported core landscape. Supported core associations in the supplied dataset are KEAP1 loss and TP53 loss with higher, less negative dependency_composite values meaning weaker composite dependency, especially H7/R7/R13 and H13/R1/R53; and SMARCA4 loss and PTEN loss with lower, more negative values meaning stronger composite dependency, especially H8/R8/R39 and H37/R24/R26. MSI-high is now a validated reverse-associated subgroup with lower values and stronger dependency, H120/R73/R92, robust in adenocarcinoma H122/R80, high-quality screens H123/R81, high mutation burden H126/R82, and central-loss-intact contexts H121/R74. The central landscape is not limited to the MSI-high minority: KEAP1 and SMARCA4 associations remain inside MSI-high H135/R88 and H136/R89, and PTEN remains inside MSI-negative H138/R91. Negative or unsupported claimed associations include KRAS H2/R2, MYC H3/R3, EGFR H4/R4, PIK3CA H5/R5, STK11 in the claimed stronger-dependency direction H6/R6 and H18/R79, ARID1A H9/R9, constructed research markers H10-H12/R10-R12, RB1 in the claimed weaker-dependency direction H38/R25, SMAD4 H39/R38, ERBB2 H40/R67 and H102/R68, BRCA2 H41/R69 and H103/R70, NF1 H42/R71 and H104/R72, APC H84/R51, BRAF V600E H85/R52, media-serum difference H107/R76, CRISPR Avana offset H24/R77, matched omics availability H25/R78, MTAP in central-loss-excluded and high-quality contexts H63/R37 and H106/R75, and several claimed interactions that failed direction-specific thresholds, including high-burden and central-loss-intact MSI interactions H127/R83 and H131/R84. Unresolved or underpowered issues remain: TP53 effect within MSI-high is too imprecise H137/R90, MSI interactions by lineage H125, by TP53 loss H128, and by small MSI strata H132-H134 remain unresolved or low priority, and several narrow PTEN or CDKN2A context estimates sit near threshold. The most informative next analysis is to use already-registered broad-context tests rather than small MSI-high subcontexts: direct KEAP1, SMARCA4, and TP53 effects in MSI-negative cells H139-H141, and formal MSI-by-lineage and MSI-by-TP53 interactions H125 and H128, to clarify homogeneity of the central landscape and the boundary conditions of the MSI-high effect. All conclusions are supplied-dataset associations under the stated eligibility/subgroup contrasts, not causal effects, single-gene knockout claims, or generalizable biological facts.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 final synthesis: H120 accepted and closed after independent validation R92, confirming MSI-high cells have stronger composite dependency. H88 rejected and closed as a threshold-level claim: discovery R57 was borderline and validation R66 shifted the signed CDKN2A-loss estimate to +0.121 with a wide lower bound, so CDKN2A is not part of the supported core landscape although small effects remain possible. Supported core landscape: KEAP1 and TP53 loss track with weaker dependency, higher/less negative values; SMARCA4 and PTEN loss track with stronger dependency, lower/more negative values; MSI-high tracks strongly with stronger dependency and is robust across central-loss exclusion, adenocarcinoma, high-quality screens, and high mutation burden. KEAP1 and SMARCA4 remain supported inside MSI-high, PTEN remains supported inside MSI-negative. Next priority is to analyze existing broad-context claims: H139-H141 for central effects in MSI-negative cells and H125/H128 for lineage and TP53 modification of the MSI-high association. Avoid additional small MSI-high subcontexts. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
