  "narrative": "I assessed the newly delivered discovery results using the signed-direction convention and the 0.15 composite-unit threshold. For negative-direction PTEN-loss, SMARCA4-loss, and MSI-high claims, a positive signed estimate means more negative dependency_composite values, i.e. stronger composite dependency; for positive-direction KEAP1-loss and TP53-loss claims, a positive signed estimate means less negative values, i.e. weaker composite dependency. Several accepted contexts remain robust in the supplied dataset. H218, MSI-high status among high-Cas9 cells, gives signed +0.793 with 95% lower bound +0.548; this clears threshold comfortably and I accept it as a within-dataset context-specific stronger-dependency association, though not as independent replication. H219, KEAP1 loss among jointly high screen-ROC and high-Cas9 cells, gives signed +0.680 with lower bound +0.500; this supports weaker composite dependency in KEAP1-loss cells even in the stringent measured assay-quality context, and I accept and close it. H222, PTEN loss in the clean TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, MSI-negative lower-screen-quality context, gives signed +0.361 with lower bound +0.183; this is threshold-supported in that context, so I accept and close it, while emphasizing that it is one overlapping PTEN context rather than proof of uniform robustness. H220, TP53 loss in jointly high screen quality and high Cas9 activity, has signed +0.358, which is directionally supportive and above threshold at the point estimate, but its lower bound is +0.126, below the 0.15 threshold; I keep it unresolved and defer further work because broad TP53-loss effects are already accepted and this stringent stratum is less central than the PTEN assay-quality questions. The PTEN results remain informative but context-sensitive. H223, PTEN loss in the clean MSI-negative higher-screen-quality context, has signed +0.227 with lower bound +0.115; H224, PTEN loss in the clean high-Cas9 context, has signed +0.217 with lower bound +0.030; and H225, PTEN loss in the clean low-Cas9 context, has signed +0.359 with lower bound +0.142. None have interval lower bounds clearing 0.15, so I cannot accept these contexts, but they are too close and too scientifically relevant to close: I leave H223, H224, and H225 unresolved and active. They suggest possible attenuation or underprecision in higher screen-quality or high-Cas9 contexts, and possible borderline support in low-Cas9 contexts, but do not establish modification. The interaction tests do not establish effect modification. H216 and H217, broader TP53-intact/SMARCA4-intact interactions, have signed +0.193 and +0.189, respectively, but both intervals include zero and have lower bounds below zero; I leave them unresolved and deferred because the point estimates are suggestive but the uncertainty is too large. H226 and H227, the cleaner PTEN-loss interactions testing stronger raw contrasts in low screen quality or low Cas9 activity, have point estimates only +0.144 and +0.146, just below threshold, with lower bounds below zero; the evidence does not support a meaningful interaction, and I close them unresolved because further discovery on the same overlapping cells is unlikely to resolve them without independent data. H228 tests PTEN attenuation in high screen quality; its signed estimate is only +0.069 with lower bound -0.110, so there is no threshold-level evidence of attenuation. I close it unresolved rather than reject because the upper bound remains above threshold and the test is imprecise. Overall, these results strengthen accepted robustness for MSI-high, KEAP1, and one clean PTEN context, while leaving PTEN context dependence and TP53 stringent-context precision as remaining uncertainty. No independent validation capacity remains, so all conclusions are descriptive associations in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, single-gene-knockout mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 14 appraise update. Independent validation capacity remains exhausted; current decisions are based only on supplied-dataset discovery evidence and are descriptive, not causal or mechanistic. Signed convention: positive signed estimates for direction -1 claims (PTEN loss, SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high) mean stronger composite dependency; positive signed estimates for direction +1 claims (KEAP1 loss, TP53 loss) mean weaker composite dependency. For interactions, positive signed estimates mean the claimed contrast difference in the stated direction is larger in the focal subgroup or in the claimed direction relative to complement.\n\nAccepted/newly accepted robust contexts: H218 MSI-high high-Cas9 signed +0.793 lower +0.548; H219 KEAP1 high screen/high Cas9 signed +0.680 lower +0.500; H222 clean PTEN low-screen-quality signed +0.361 lower +0.183. These should be reported as within-dataset context associations, not independent replications, because samples overlap and are not independent.\n\nUnresolved PTEN context tests: H223 clean high-screen-quality signed +0.227 lower +0.115; H224 clean high-Cas9 signed +0.217 lower +0.030; H225 clean low-Cas9 signed +0.359 lower +0.142. H223 and H224 are important possible attenuation/underprecision contexts and remain active. H225 is near threshold but not cleared; it remains active rather than accepted. H220 TP53 high screen/high Cas9 signed +0.358 lower +0.126 is unresolved and deferred because broad TP53-loss is already strongly accepted and this is a smaller precision issue.\n\nInteraction results do not establish modifier effects: H216/H217 broad PTEN interactions are suggestive but imprecise and are deferred; H226/H227 clean low-screen/low-Cas9 interactions are just below threshold with intervals crossing zero and are closed unresolved; H228 high-screen PTEN attenuation interaction is small and imprecise and is closed unresolved. No scientifically meaningful interaction or epistasis effect has been established.\n\nScientific interpretation: KEAP1 loss, TP53 loss, SMARCA4 loss, and MSI-high remain large accepted within-dataset associations. PTEN loss remains a moderate accepted association overall, supported in several clean and some broad contexts, but it is not uniformly threshold-cleared across assay-quality strata and its interaction modification remains unsupported. Multiplicity and overlapping contexts are serious limitations, especially for PTEN; accepted PTEN contexts should not be treated as independent confirmations. Next priorities: leave H223, H224, H225 active for PTEN context uncertainty, defer broad TP53 stringent-context precision, and avoid further low-priority signature/marker/small-interaction exploration unless a new independent data source or scheduled validation becomes available."
}

