  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation capacity is exhausted, so these are supplied-dataset discovery proposals. The main scientific uncertainty is PTEN loss: broad and many clean contexts support a moderate association between PTEN loss and stronger composite dependency, but several stringent assay-quality contexts have point estimates near or below the 0.15-unit threshold. These proposals test whether PTEN loss retains a credible threshold-supported association when major co-occurring predictors are removed and measured editing/screening quality is varied. They also ask whether PTEN effects are genuinely modified by Cas9 activity or screen quality, rather than merely varying because of co-occurrence, cell-line composition, or imprecision. The endpoint is dependency_composite; more negative values mean stronger composite dependency. For PTEN-loss and SMARCA4-loss claims with direction -1, a positive signed estimate means a more negative raw contrast, i.e. stronger dependency; for KEAP1-loss and TP53-loss claims with direction +1, a positive signed estimate means a less negative raw contrast, i.e. weaker dependency. For PTEN interactions, I anticipate raw attenuation in high Cas9 activity or high screen quality: the raw PTEN-loss contrast should be less negative in those high-quality strata than in their complements, so those interaction claims are direction +1 with anticipated_direction +1. For low Cas9 activity or low screen quality, I anticipate raw PTEN-loss associations to be more negative than in the complement, so those interaction claims are direction -1 with anticipated_direction -1. If high-quality attenuation interactions have intervals crossing zero or lower bounds not credibly above the signed threshold, the correct conclusion is no established effect modification, even if main effects are accepted. The KEAP1, TP53, and SMARCA4 clean high-Cas9 proposals are falsifiable persistence checks: if a major accepted predictor becomes non-threshold or implausibly attenuated after removing TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1/PTEN/MSI contexts, it would indicate context dependence or confounding by co-occurring predictor status rather than a uniform within-dataset association. All inferences remain descriptive associations in the supplied overlapping dataset, not causal, mechanistic single-gene-knockout claims, or externally generalizable conclusions.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 explore update. No assessments are due and no independent validation requests remain. Current accepted large within-dataset associations are KEAP1 loss (direction +1, weaker dependency), TP53 loss (direction +1, weaker dependency), SMARCA4 loss (direction -1, stronger dependency), and MSI-high status (direction -1, stronger dependency). PTEN loss is accepted as a moderate stronger-dependency association overall and in many clean contexts, but it is less uniformly threshold-cleared, especially in high Cas9 activity and some high screen-quality strata. H145 already accepted PTEN loss among TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, KEAP1-intact, MSI-negative, high-screen-quality cells; therefore new PTEN proposals avoid duplicating that exact clean high-screen main effect. New focus: clean PTEN effects stratified by high Cas9, low Cas9, and low screen quality after removing TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1/MSI contexts; clean PTEN interactions testing high-Cas9 or high-screen attenuation and low-Cas9 or low-screen stronger associations; and clean high-Cas9 main effects for KEAP1, TP53, and SMARCA4 after removing the other major predictors/MSI. These are overlapping supplied-dataset contexts, not independent replications. Interactions remain difficult to establish because of sample-size and multiplicity limitations; accept only if signed estimates and intervals credibly exceed 0.15 in the claimed direction. Conclusions remain descriptive associations in this dataset, not causal/mechanistic or generalizable claims."
