  "narrative": "For direction -1 PTEN-loss claims, a positive signed estimate means the raw PTEN-loss exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative, i.e. PTEN-loss samples have more negative dependency_composite scores and thus stronger composite dependency. The outcome threshold is +0.15 signed composite-unit effect in the claimed direction, and acceptance should also be supported by the interval, not only the point estimate. H241 (clean top-screen-quality cells) is directionally supportive: +0.232, 95% CI +0.087 to +0.377. The point estimate exceeds the threshold, but the interval lower bound is below it and the cells are small, so this is retained as unresolved rather than accepted; it is deferred because it is an overlapping PTEN context and validation capacity is exhausted. H242 (PTEN loss in low mutation burden) is similar: +0.207, CI +0.010 to +0.405. The point estimate is above threshold but the uncertainty includes very modest effects, so it is unresolved and deferred. H243 (PTEN loss in high ploidy) has +0.162, CI -0.046 to +0.370. Although the point estimate slightly exceeds threshold, the interval includes null and sub-threshold values, so it is unresolved and deferred as an imprecise context rather than evidence of a meaningful PTEN effect in that subgroup. H244 (PTEN loss in low growth rate) has +0.137, CI -0.075 to +0.348; the point estimate itself is below the meaningfulness threshold and the interval includes null, so it is rejected and closed. H245 (PTEN loss in high growth rate) is the strongest new PTEN context: +0.331, CI +0.144 to +0.518. The point estimate is well above threshold, but the lower bound is just below +0.15. This is scientifically intriguing and not null, but it does not credibly clear the threshold at 95% confidence, so I keep it unresolved and active while registering a refinement that restricts to high growth rate and simultaneously removes major co-occurring predictors (TP53-, SMARCA4-, KEAP1-, MSI-negative) to assess whether the apparent high-growth PTEN signal survives confounding/co-occurrence and cell-count pressure. Interaction tests remain negative: H239 tests attenuation of PTEN contrast in high screen-quality subgroup relative to complement (direction +1), but estimates +0.148 with CI -0.047 to +0.342, below threshold and compatible with no effect modification, so it is rejected. H246 tests low-Cas9 strengthening of PTEN effect (direction -1), estimates +0.189 with CI -0.048 to +0.425; although the point estimate is above threshold, the interval crosses null and does not credibly support interaction, so it is rejected. H247 tests high-screen-quality attenuation, estimates -0.006 with CI -0.227 to +0.215, essentially null, and is rejected. I also deferred H190, H223, and H229, which are overlapping PTEN contexts with supportive point estimates but intervals including sub-threshold values. Broad conclusions remain unchanged: KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker composite dependency, TP53 loss with weaker dependency, SMARCA4 loss with stronger dependency, MSI-high with stronger dependency, and broad PTEN loss with moderate stronger dependency; the PTEN context dependence remains unresolved. These are descriptive within-dataset associations, not causal, mechanistic, single-gene knockout, or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 16 appraise. Validation capacity remains exhausted, so no validation request. New PTEN robustness results do not add accepted contexts: H241, H242, H243, and H245 are directionally supportive but have lower bounds below +0.15 and are therefore unresolved. H244 and the new PTEN-by-quality/Cas9/screen interactions H239, H246, H247 are rejected/closed. Active focus is narrowed to PTEN in high growth rate (H245) and a proposed clean high-growth refinement removing TP53-, SMARCA4-, KEAP1-, and MSI-high co-predictors. Previously active PTEN contexts H190, H223, and H229 are deferred because they are overlapping, imprecise, and unlikely to become decisive without new validation. Accepted main within-dataset associations remain unchanged: KEAP1 loss weaker dependency, TP53 loss weaker dependency, SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency, MSI-high stronger dependency, and broad PTEN loss moderate stronger dependency, with accepted selected PTEN contexts from earlier iterations. No tested interaction establishes effect modification by screen quality, Cas9, ploidy, mutation burden, growth rate, major co-predictors, lineage, culture, or constructed research assays. All conclusions are descriptive associations in the supplied dataset."
