  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered and no validation response deadline is pending; validation capacity is exhausted. I therefore synthesized the final evidence from the supplied dataset and available validation, tightened overlapping context claims, and left one focused untested PTEN refinement active. Strongly supported within-dataset associations are: KEAP1 loss associated with weaker composite dependency, signed +0.832 in discovery (95% CI +0.766 to +0.897) and +0.826 in validation (CI +0.735 to +0.917; H7, R7/R13); SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency, signed +0.833 (CI +0.767 to +0.898) and +0.845 in validation (CI +0.752 to +0.939; H8, R8/R39); TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency, signed +0.423 (CI +0.327 to +0.520) and +0.356 in validation (CI +0.214 to +0.498; H13, R1/R53); and MSI-high associated with stronger dependency, signed +0.792 (CI +0.676 to +0.907) and +0.802 in validation (CI +0.635 to +0.969; H120, R73/R92). PTEN loss is a moderate but real within-dataset stronger-dependency association, signed +0.227 (CI +0.131 to +0.323) and validation +0.281 (CI +0.135 to +0.428; H37, R24/R26). Selected clean or stratified PTEN contexts are also accepted, including clean high-screen-quality cells H145 (R99/R105), broad clean co-predictor cells H149 (R107/R119), clean TP53/SMARCA4/MSI-negative cells H177 (R139/R145), and lower screen-quality cells H196 (R192). Independent validation of H145, H149, and H177 reinforces the direction of PTEN association, although several PTEN validation intervals are too imprecise to make strong subgroup claims. TP53 loss in lower screen-quality MSI-negative cells is supported in both discovery and validation (H170, R122/R132). Negative findings include main effects for KRAS H2, MYC H3, EGFR H4, PIK3CA H5, STK11 main H6, STK11 in KEAP1-intact cells H18, ARID1A H9, RB1 H38, ERBB2 H40, BRCA2 H41, NF1 H42, APC H84, BRAF H85, MTAP in clean contexts H63/H97/H106, constructed markers H10-H12, media serum 10 percent vs 5 percent H107, Avana library H24, matched RNA/DNA availability H25, and batch_a vs batch_b H176. Tested interaction contrasts do not establish effect modification by screen quality, Cas9 activity, ploidy, mutation burden, growth rate, major co-predictors, lineage, culture, or constructed signatures; representative rejected interactions include H216, H217, H226, H227, H232, H233, H235, H239, H246, H247, and H81. The principal unresolved issue is PTEN context dependence. High-growth PTEN cells H245 (signed +0.331, CI +0.144 to +0.518) and low-Cas9 PTEN cells H198 (signed +0.339, CI +0.131 to +0.547) are directionally supportive but do not credibly clear the 0.15 threshold because their lower bounds fall below it; they are deferred rather than accepted or rejected as independent contexts. Related PTEN contexts H241, H242, H243, H190, H223, H229, H237, and H220 are closed as overlapping imprecise contexts, leaving H248 as the single most informative active analysis: PTEN loss in high growth-rate cells among TP53-intact, SMARCA4-intact, KEAP1-intact, MSI-negative samples. If H248 clears the threshold, PTEN dependency in high growth rate may be accepted as a within-dataset context; if it remains below threshold, PTEN apparent context dependence is better interpreted as composition, co-occurrence, or imprecision rather than robust effect modification. CDKN2A remains borderline and unresolved because point estimates are near but not reliably above threshold. All conclusions are descriptive associations in this dataset and do not establish causality, single-gene knockout mechanism, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.",
